    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 81.88 score. His matchup against Gray is exceptionally favorable, bolstered by a 16% park factor lift and a 14% platoon advantage that outweighs the SP skill tax. We are also leaning heavily into **Heliot Ramos** (62.21) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.14); the former benefits significantly from the 4.90 xERA of Ray, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-ceiling matchup against Lugo that remains a \"Strong\" play despite a minor platoon efficiency dip. **Miguel Vargas** also warrants attention; while his score of 50.34 is modest, his 100% stolen base opportunity against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him a vital, high-upside asset in our pursuit of league-leading SB totals.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Liam Hicks** (39.70). He fell just short of our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" due to a brutal encounter with deGrom, whose elite 3.15 xERA and skill profile negated the positive platoon bump and cleanup order slot. While **Liam Hicks** was the closest to a start, his inability to clear the threshold keeps him on the pine alongside **Wade Meckler**, who similarly suffered from a subpar matchup against Ashcraft. Our primary risks today revolve around our catchers and corner infielders facing high-tier arms: **Drake Baldwin** faces the formidable Wheeler, dragging his score to a marginal 49.38, while **Dominic Smith** remains a borderline start (42.10) whose limited upside is propped up only by a favorable BvP history. We remain diligent in monitoring the remaining lineup confirmations for players like **Jordan Westburg** or **Coby Mayo** to ensure no bench-worthy assets are left on the table during this late-season push.",
